{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-02T06:27:33.513Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 2 is implemented and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\n**New `src/watcher/provider-retry.ts`** holds the provider decision:\n- `decideProviderRetry` waits `gates.providerRetryDelaySeconds` since the latest `dead` event and caps retries at `gates.providerRetries`, counted from automatic `retry` events with `reason: provider_unavailable` since the later of approval and the last manual retry. The clock is injected (`now`).\n- Also exports the event-stream helpers and `PROVIDER_REASON` / `PROVIDER_DEFAULTS`.\n\n**`src/watcher/auto-retry.ts`** (now 201 lines, `decideDeadTask` 53):\n- `provider_unavailable` is eligible, but never goes through the stuck check.\n- `automaticRetriesSince` skips provider retries so they never spend `gates.autoRetries`.\n- `runAutomaticRetries` and `decideDeadTask` take an optional injected `now` (default `Date.now()`), so tests cross the wait without sleeping.\n\n**`tests/provider-retry.test.ts`** covers the wait, the separate budget under `gates.autoRetries: 1` (two same-fingerprint provider deaths never stuck, followed by a `verify_red` death that still retries), budget exhaustion, `gates.autoRetries: 0`, and the retained stuck behaviour for other reasons — all through `runAutomaticRetries` against a temporary change folder, plus direct `decideProviderRetry` unit tests.\n\n**`README.md`** documents `provider_unavailable` in the Automatic retry and Stuck tasks bullets, a new Provider outages bullet for the early SIGTERM stop, all three `gates.provider*` defaults, and the dead reasons list.\n\nVerification:\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/provider-retry.test.ts`: 8/8 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: exit 0 (typechecks, build, full test suite, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/136-provider-outage-deaths/.run/results/2.md`."}}
